Turen fuzzy-hash is a bounded WebAssembly hashing wrapper that combines the
following pure-Rust crates from crates.io:

- fuzzyhash 0.2.2 (https://github.com/rustysec/fuzzyhash-rs), MIT —
  ssdeep-compatible context-triggered piecewise hashing and comparison.
- tlsh2 1.1.0 (https://github.com/vthib/tlsh), Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause —
  Trend Micro TLSH similarity hashing and difference scoring.
- goblin 0.10.7 (https://github.com/m4b/goblin), MIT — PE import table parsing
  for the imphash computation. Only the PE parsers are enabled.
- md-5 0.11.0, sha1 0.11.0, sha2 0.11.0 (https://github.com/RustCrypto/hashes),
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- blake3 1.8.7 (https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3),
  CC0-1.0 OR Apache-2.0 OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception; the Apache-2.0
  option is elected for this distribution.
- xxhash-rust 0.8.18 (https://github.com/DoumanAsh/xxhash-rust), BSL-1.0
  (Boost Software License 1.0, permissive) — xxHash64 only.
- serde 1.0.228, serde_json 1.0.145, wasm-bindgen 0.2.108 and their transitive
  dependencies, MIT OR Apache-2.0 (memchr: Unlicense OR MIT; ryu:
  Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0; unicode-ident: MIT OR Apache-2.0 AND Unicode-3.0;
  constant_time_eq: CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0 OR Apache-2.0).

The complete pinned dependency set is recorded in Cargo.lock. No GPL or
copyleft code is linked into the distributed module.

The compiled module uses Rust standard-library components, distributed under
the Apache-2.0 or MIT license at the user's option.
